meta {
  name: Promote a wishlist entry
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}{{apiPrefix}}/me/wishlist/{{wishlistItemId}}/promote
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "system": "Nintendo Switch"
  }
}

docs {
  Moves a wishlist entry into the library: the game is created and the wishlist row
  removed in one transaction. Returns the new library game, unrated and with no
  sessions.

  `system` is required by the games table, so it must arrive here when the wishlist
  row never had one. When both exist the payload wins, since you might buy it on a
  different platform than you wishlisted.

  The one RPC-shaped route in the collection. It is a verb on a URL rather than a
  state change on a resource, which is the tradeoff for getting the create and the
  delete under one transaction.

  - 201 the new library game
  - 403 library at MAX_GAMES
  - 404 no such wishlist entry
  - 409 that game is already in the library
  - 422 no system anywhere
  - 429 over the write budget
}
